@Server_HostAddress = http://localhost:5346

### Begin provider login (open in a browser — this returns a 302 to Keycloak)
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/auth/provider/login

###

### Begin patient login (open in a browser — this returns a 302 to Keycloak)
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/auth/patient/login

###

### Begin owner login (open in a browser — this returns a 302 to Keycloak)
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/auth/owner/login

###

### Keycloak application-initiated action (password, 2FA, email) — needs that realm's
### session cookie, so open in a signed-in browser. 302 to Keycloak with kc_action;
### 400 for an action outside UPDATE_PASSWORD, CONFIGURE_TOTP, UPDATE_EMAIL.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/auth/provider/action/UPDATE_PASSWORD?returnUrl=/provider/account/security

###

GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/auth/patient/action/CONFIGURE_TOTP?returnUrl=/patient/account/security

###

### Current session (requires the __Host-anamnys-provider, __Host-anamnys-patient
### or __Host-anamnys-owner cookie — send from a browser session, not this file)
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me

###

### End the provider session
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/auth/provider/logout

###

### End the patient session
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/auth/patient/logout

###

### End the owner session
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/auth/owner/logout

###

### Own profile (needs the matching realm's session cookie — send from a signed-in browser)
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/profile

###

PUT {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ana Souza", "crpNumber": "06/12345", "crpRegion": "SP" }

###

GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/patients/me/profile

###

PUT {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/patients/me/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Ana", "lastName": "Souza", "phone": "+55 11 91234-5678", "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-02" }

###
### Note detail (requires the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie — send from a browser session, not this file)
### Status, raw transcript and failure reason of one note. Replace the id with a real note id.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

###
### Restructure note (requires the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie — send from a browser session, not this file)
### Re-runs the AI structuring of a ReadyForReview note; format is DAP, SOAP or Biopsychosocial. 202 accepted, 409 if signed/pending/edited.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/restructure
Content-Type: application/json

{ "format": "SOAP" }

###
### Edit note section (requires the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie — send from a browser session, not this file)
### Saves the section text. 200 { revision }; 409 reason "locked" (pending/signed) or "stale" (revision mismatch); 400 if content is null or over 20000 characters.
PUT {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/sections/data
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "Texto da seção.", "expectedRevision": 0 }

###
### Create blank sections (requires the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie — send from a browser session, not this file)
### Creates the empty sections of the note's format when it has none. 201 created, 409 if locked or it already has sections.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/sections/blank

###
### Sign note (requires the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie — send from a browser session, not this file)
### Signs a ReadyForReview note with the provider's CRP. 200 signed; 409 reason "locked" or "no_sections"; 422 reason "missing_crp".
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/sign

###
### Create a typed note (requires the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie — send from a browser session, not this file)
### Mode "ai" organises the text into sections (201 { noteId }, structuring runs in the background); "manual" creates empty sections. 400 on invalid body; 404 unknown patient/appointment; 409 code "archived" or "appointment_unavailable".
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "appointmentId": null,
  "format": "DAP",
  "mode": "ai",
  "text": "Paciente relata dificuldade para dormir há duas semanas."
}

###
### Appointments of a patient that can receive a typed note (requires the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie — send from a browser session, not this file)
### Last 14 days, not cancelled, without a note. 200 array newest first; 404 for an unknown patient.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/note-candidates

###
### Search the provider's notes (requires the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie - send from a browser session, not this file)
### Filters live in the body: patient names never go in a URL. status: pending | signed | failed (omit for all); termId: theme term (signed notes tagged with it or a child; unknown -> 400); 25 per page, newest first; 200 { items, hasMore }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "pending",
  "patientId": null,
  "name": null,
  "page": 1,
  "termId": null
}

###

### Export a signed note as PDF (returns a presigned URL valid for 1 hour)
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/export

###

### Psychometric scales (all require the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie - send from a browser session, not this file)
### Instruments with the provider-specific regime: available | needs_opt_in | opted_in | unavailable. 200 array of 15.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/instruments

###
### Opt in to a "sem classificacao" instrument. 204; 404 unknown; 409 opt_in_not_allowed.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/instruments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/opt-in

###
### Scale series of a patient, grouped by instrument; optional sessionId filter. 200 array; 404 unknown patient.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/scales?sessionId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

###
### Record a score (score and date only). 201 { id }; 400 validation; 404; 409 archived | instrument_unavailable | opt_in_required.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/scales
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "instrumentId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "score": 12,
  "appliedAt": "2026-10-18T12:00:00Z",
  "sessionId": null
}

###
### Remove a recorded score (soft removal). 204; 404.
DELETE {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/scales/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

###
### Psychological documents (all require the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie - send from a browser session, not this file)
### Available kinds with their ruleset elements and prohibitions. 200 array of 3.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/document-kinds

###
### Document check mode. 200 { documentCheckMode }.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/document-settings

###
### Change the check mode (blocking | advisory). 200; 400 on other values.
PUT {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/document-settings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "documentCheckMode": "advisory"
}

###
### Documents of a patient, newest first. 200 array; 404 unknown patient.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/documents

###
### Create a draft. 201 { id }; 404; 409 archived | kind_not_available.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/documents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "declaracao",
  "noteId": null
}

###
### Document detail with the conformity check. 200; 404.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

###
### Save a draft. 200 detail; 400 field too long; 404; 409 locked.
PUT {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fields": { "finalidade": "" },
  "confirmations": []
}

###
### Save a relatorio_multiprofissional draft with its team (max 10 members; name 200, category 100, registry 50, analysis 20000 chars; empty members are dropped). 200 detail with team[]; 400 team | team[i].name|category|registry|analysis; 400 team on any other kind; 404; 409 locked.
PUT {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fields": { "finalidade": "" },
  "confirmations": [],
  "team": [
    { "name": "Rita Lima", "category": "Psiquiatria", "registry": "CRM 12345", "analysis": "" }
  ]
}

###
### Sign. 200; 404; 409 locked | missing_elements | confirmations_required (+ missing[]); 422 missing_crp | missing_city.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/sign
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acknowledgeMissing": false
}

###
### Correct a signed document (new draft copy). 201 { id }; 404; 409 locked | archived.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/correct

###
### Export a signed document as PDF (presigned URL valid for 1 hour). 200 { url, expiresAt }; 404; 409 not_signed; 503 storage_unavailable.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/export###
### Search the provider's documents. Filters live in the body: patient names never go in a URL. status: draft | signed | superseded (omit for all); 25 per page, newest first; 200 { items, hasMore }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/documents/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "signed",
  "patientId": null,
  "name": null,
  "page": 1
}


###
### Theme vocabulary (all require the __Host-anamnys-provider cookie - send from a browser session, not this file)
### All terms of the active vocabulary. 200 [{ id, code, label, parentId, status, successorIds }].
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/theme-vocabulary

###
### Active themes of a note. 200 [{ id, termId, code, label, parentLabel, termStatus, origin, proposed, addedAt }]; 404 unknown note.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/themes

###
### Tag a note (drafts and signed notes). fromSuggestion marks an accepted AI suggestion. 201 { id }; 400 without termId; 404; 409 term_inactive | already_tagged | archived.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/themes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "termId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "fromSuggestion": false
}

###
### Suggest themes with the in-process model (writes nothing; terms already tagged are excluded). 200 { terms: [{ id, code, label }] } ({ terms: [] } for a note without text); 404; 503 suggest_failed.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/themes/suggest

###
### Remove a theme from a note (soft removal). 204; 404 unknown or already removed; 409 archived.
DELETE {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/themes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


###
### Passage behind a reference (theme excerpt). 200 { id, kind: exact|section, noteId, patientId, sessionStartsAt, datedAt, sectionKey, sectionTitle, sectionText, start?, end? } (start/end only for exact); 401; 404 unknown or other provider's.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/excerpts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

###
### Theme vocabulary admin (owners cookie __Host-anamnys-owner; provider cookie = 401). Reads: any staff role. Mutations: owner or ops (support = 403). Conflicts 409 { code }, input errors 400.
### Terms of the active vocabulary. 200 [{ id, code, label, parentId, status, introducedOn, successorIds, activeTagCount }].
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/admin/theme-vocabulary

###
### New term (code ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{1,59}$, label 1-80, optional parentId = active top-level term). 201 { id }; 400; 409 code_taken.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/admin/theme-vocabulary/terms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "novo_tema",
  "label": "Novo tema",
  "parentId": null
}

###
### Rename (label only; id and code never change). 204; 400; 404; 409 term_not_active.
PUT {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/admin/theme-vocabulary/terms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/label
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Novo rótulo"
}

###
### Retire an active term. 204; 404; 409 term_not_active | has_active_children. Tags stay.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/admin/theme-vocabulary/terms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/retire

###
### Split into 2-10 new terms under the same parent; the old term becomes superseded. 200 { ids }; 400; 404; 409 term_not_active | code_taken.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/admin/theme-vocabulary/terms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/split
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "terms": [
    { "code": "parte_um", "label": "Parte um" },
    { "code": "parte_dois", "label": "Parte dois" }
  ]
}

###
### Merge 2-10 active terms of the same level into an existing term (target.existingId) or a new one (target.code + label). 200 { id } of the target; 400; 404; 409 term_not_active | level_mismatch | code_taken.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/admin/theme-vocabulary/merge
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceIds": ["00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"],
  "target": { "code": "tema_unificado", "label": "Tema unificado" }
}

###
### Full account export (provider cookie __Host-anamnys-provider; send from a browser session, not this file). One export in progress per provider.
### Request an export. 202 { id, status: "queued" }; 409 { code: "export_in_progress" }. The ZIP is built in the background; the bell notifies when ready.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/exports

###
### Latest export. 200 { id, status: queued | running | done | failed | expired, requestedAt, completedAt, sizeBytes, expiresAt }; 204 when none.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/exports

###
### One-hour download link (a new link on every call). 200 { url, expiresAt }; 404 unknown or another provider's export; 409 { code: "not_ready" | "expired" }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/exports/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/download

###
### External documents (F-07; provider cookie __Host-anamnys-provider; send from a browser session, not this file). PDF/JPG/PNG up to 20 MB, scanned by ClamAV before it can be opened.
### Upload (multipart: file, kind = laudo | receita | exame | encaminhamento | relatorio_externo | outro, documentDate? yyyy-MM-dd, description? <= 200). 201 { id, scanStatus: "pending" }; 400 { code: unsupported_type | too_large | type_mismatch | empty | invalid_form } or validation problem; 404; 409 { code: "archived" }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/external-documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----b

------b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="kind"

laudo
------b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="laudo.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

%PDF-1.4
------b--

###
### A patient's documents, newest first. 200 [{ id, patientId, patientName: null, fileName, kind, documentDate, description, scanStatus: pending | clean | infected | failed, byteSize, uploadedAt, scannedAt }]; 404.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/external-documents

###
### Provider-wide search (patient name in the body, 25 per page). 200 { items (with patientName), hasMore }; 400 validation problem.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "kind": "exame", "patientId": null, "name": "maria", "page": 1 }

###
### One-hour inline link, audited. 200 { url, expiresAt }; 404; 409 { code: "not_available" } unless the scan is clean.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/open

###
### Soft delete (the object is removed). 204; 404; 409 { code: "archived" }.
DELETE {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

###
### Declared facts of an external document (F-08). List and search items also carry readStatus (null | pending | reading | done | failed), pendingFacts and extracting.
### Facts under review (discarded left out). 200 { documentId, readStatus, pageCount, pagesTruncated, extracting, facts: [{ id, kind: issuer | registration | issue_date | icd | medication | conclusion, value, correctedValue, page, quote, status: pending | confirmed | corrected, excerptRefId, createdAt, confirmedAt, recorded (a medication record was made from it) }] }; 404.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/facts

###
### Confirm a pending fact. 204 (also when already confirmed); 404; 409 { code: "not_pending" | "archived" }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/facts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/confirm

###
### Correct a fact (kept next to what was read; the kind's format applies: ICD X00 / X00.0, a real date, council acronym + number). 204; 400 validation problem { value }; 404; 409 { code: "not_pending" (discarded) | "archived" }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/facts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/correct
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": "F43.1" }

###
### Discard a fact (soft). 204; 404; 409 { code: "archived" }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/facts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/discard

###
### "Ler de novo": extract again (read done; reviewed facts kept) or read again (read failed; attempts reset). 202 { readStatus }; 404; 409 { code: "archived" | "not_available" (not scanned clean) }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/extract

###
### Confirmed and corrected facts of a patient's documents, newest document first. 200 [{ id, documentId, documentKind, documentDate, uploadedAt, kind, value (the correction when corrected), readValue, corrected, page, quote, excerptRefId, confirmedAt }]; 404.
### The passage behind a fact: GET providers/me/excerpts/{excerptRefId} returns { id, sourceType: "document", kind, documentId, documentKind, patientId, datedAt, pageNumber, pageText, start, end }.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/declared-facts

###
### Medication from a fact (F-09). Prefill for a medication fact (not discarded) plus the patient's active records of the same drug (case/accent-insensitive).
### 200 { factId, value, quote, page, status, recorded, prefill: { drug, dose, posology, startedOn, endedOn }, activeMatches: [{ id, treatmentId, drug, dose, posology, startedOn }] }; 404; 409 { code: "not_medication" | "not_pending" (discarded) }.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/facts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/medication-draft

###
### Save the medication in one transaction, confirming the fact (or correcting it when the text differs from what was read). action: "new" | "dose_change" (closes targetMedicationId the day before startedOn and opens a record of the same treatment) | "stop" (targetMedicationId + endedOn; drug/dose/posology/startedOn ignored).
### 201 { id } (the new record; the target for "stop"); 400 validation problem { action | drug | dose | posology | startedOn | endedOn | targetMedicationId }; 404 (also a target of another patient); 409 { code: "archived" | "not_pending" | "not_medication" | "already_recorded" | "target_not_active" }. Audited as medication_from_fact (ids and action only).
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/external-documents/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/facts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/medication
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "new", "targetMedicationId": null, "drug": "Sertralina", "dose": "50 mg", "posology": "1 comprimido pela manhã", "startedOn": "2026-09-14", "endedOn": null }

###
### Timeline of a patient: medication lanes (one per treatment, a segment per record) and scale series, dates only. from/to (yyyy-MM-dd) are optional; segments and points outside the period are left out. 400 when from is after to.
### Also appointments: [{ id, on, kind }] (kind: attended | attended_unscheduled | no_show | cancelled_provider | cancelled_patient | unrecorded; past only, same period).
### 200 { medications: [{ treatmentId, drug, segments: [{ medicationId, dose, posology, startedOn, endedOn, origin: { kind: "manual" | "document" | "document_deleted", documentId, documentKind, documentDate, page, excerptId } }] }], scales: [{ instrumentId, code, name, minScore, maxScore, points: [{ applicationId, score, appliedOn }] }] }; 404.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/timeline?from=2026-04-26&to=2026-10-26

###
### Attendance statistics of a patient (design/specs/2026-10-27-attendance-stats-design.md §3), dates only. from/to (yyyy-MM-dd, practice-local day) are optional; only events up to now. 400 when from is after to; 404 for another provider's patient.
### 200 { counts: { attended, attendedUnscheduled, noShow, cancelledByProvider, cancelledByPatient, unrecorded }, cancellationLeadHours: { median, min, max, count } | null, intervalDays: { median, min, max, last } | null, daysSinceLast: number | null }
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/attendance?from=2025-10-26&to=2026-10-26

###
### Compliance panel (F-06, design/specs/2026-10-28-retention-panel-design.md §3). Three lists, each by date, provider-scoped, discarded patients left out.
### unsignedNotes: notes without a signature at least unsignedNoteDays practice days old, oldest first. retention: deadline within 90 days or past, earliest first (expired = the deadline day has gone by; hasFutureAppointment = scheduled/confirmed after now).
### documents: drafts (missing = what the current ruleset/profile still lacks) and signed documents whose signature check did not pass (status "signed"), oldest first; superseded ones left out.
### 200 { unsignedNotes: [{ noteId, patientId, patientName, createdAt, ageDays }], retention: [{ patientId, patientName, lastRecordAt, retentionUntil, expired, hasFutureAppointment }], documents: [{ documentId, patientId, patientName, kind, status: "draft" | "signed", missing: [elementCode], createdAt }] }
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/compliance

###
### Retention settings ("Guarda"). 200 { guardYears, unsignedNoteDays } (defaults 5 and 7).
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/settings/retention

###
### Save them. guardYears 5..100 (Res. CFP 001/2009 minimum), unsignedNoteDays 1..365. Changing guardYears recomputes the provider's deadlines in the same transaction.
### 204; 400 validation problem { guardYears | unsignedNoteDays }.
PUT {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/settings/retention
Content-Type: application/json

{ "guardYears": 6, "unsignedNoteDays": 7 }

###
### Discard an expired record (irreversible). Only when the deadline day has gone by and no appointment is scheduled/confirmed after now; confirmName is the patient's full name (trimmed, case- and accent-insensitive).
### One transaction deletes the clinical content, stores the disposal term PDF and audits patient_discarded (ids and counts); the stored objects go after the commit.
### 200 { termId, counts: { notes, clinicalDocuments, externalDocuments, sessions, appointments, transcripts, ... } }; 404; 409 { code: "not_expired" | "future_appointment" | "name_mismatch" | "already_discarded" }; 503 { code: "storage_unavailable" }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/discard
Content-Type: application/json

{ "confirmName": "Ana Silva" }

###
### Disposal terms, oldest first. 200 [{ id, patientId, patientName, createdAt, periodFrom, periodTo, guardYears, retentionUntil, basis, counts }]
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/disposal-terms

###
### Signed link to a term's PDF (1 hour). 200 { url, expiresAt }; 404.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/disposal-terms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/pdf

###
### Case analysis of a patient (F-10, design/specs/2026-10-28-case-analysis-design.md §3). from/to (yyyy-MM-dd, practice-local day) optional. 400 when from is after to; 404 for another provider's or a discarded patient.
### 200 { available, signedSessions, minimumSessions: 6, sessions: [{ noteId, on, sessionId?, appointmentId? }], themes: [{ termId, code, label, parentId?, active, supersededBy: [{ termId, label }], occurrences: [{ noteId, on, excerptId?, section?, quote? }] }], cooccurrence: [{ a, b, sessions }] }
### With fewer than 6 signed notes in the period, available is false and only available, signedSessions and minimumSessions are filled.
### F-12 adds absences: [{ termId, code, label, parentId?, recordedIn, spanSessions, firstOn, lastOn, sessionsSince, daysSince, lastOccurrence: { noteId, excerptId?, section?, quote? } }] and absenceSessions (N), always over the patient's whole signed history (not the period), ordered by lastOn; empty when available is false.
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/analysis?from=2025-10-28&to=2026-10-28

###
### Analysis settings (F-12). 200 { absenceSessions } (default 4).
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/settings/analysis

###
### Save them. absenceSessions 2..20: consecutive signed sessions without a record after which a theme recorded in at least 3 sessions is listed as absent.
### 204; 400 validation problem { absenceSessions }.
PUT {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/settings/analysis
Content-Type: application/json

{ "absenceSessions": 4 }

###
### Plan adherence (F-14, design/specs/2026-10-30-plan-adherence-design.md §3). 404 for another provider's or a discarded patient.
### 200 { plan: { planId?, reviewedAt? }, objectives: [{ objectiveId, description, createdAt, term?: { termId, label }, firstOn?, lastOn?, lastNoteId?, sessionsSince?, daysSince? }],
###       followUps: [{ id, description, createdAt, noteId?, excerpt?: { excerptId, section, quote }, resolvedAt?, resolvedNoteId?, sessionsSince, originOn? }] }
### Objectives of the open plan by createdAt; a theme counts when the term or a descendant was recorded in a signed note (confirmed tags, F-10 session date).
### Never recorded: first/last null, sessionsSince/daysSince counted from the definition. No term: all five null.
### Follow-ups: open first (oldest first), then resolved (latest resolution first).
GET {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/plan-adherence

###
### Mark the open plan as reviewed now (creates the plan when there is none). Audited plan_reviewed (patient and plan ids).
### 200 { planId, reviewedAt }; 404; 409 { code: "archived" }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/plan/review

###
### Objectives accept an optional theme: termId, an active term of the active vocabulary (the one the objective already has stays accepted). 400 { termId } otherwise. Writes on an archived patient: 409 { code: "archived" }.
### The patient detail lists objectives as { id, description, createdAt, termId?, termLabel? }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/objectives
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "Dormir melhor", "termId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000" }

###
### Mark a point "para retomar" on a note. Passage optional: { sectionKey, offsetStart, offsetEnd } (selection), { sectionKey } (section) or { quote }.
### Only on notes in review or signed. A quote that is not found is refused.
### 201 { id }; 400 { description | offsetStart | quote } (code "invalid_selection" when the passage does not match); 404; 409 { code: "archived" | "note_not_ready" }. Audited follow_up_created (note and follow-up ids).
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/notes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/follow-ups
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "Retomar a relação com o pai", "sectionKey": "evolucao", "offsetStart": 0, "offsetEnd": 20 }

###
### Resolve it, from a later note of the same patient ("retomada nesta nota", not the origin note nor one dated before it) or from the plan card (no noteId). 204 (also when already resolved);
### 400 { noteId } with code "invalid_note"; 404; 409 { code: "archived" }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/follow-ups/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/resolve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "noteId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000" }

###
### Reopen a resolved one. 204 (also when already open); 404; 409 { code: "archived" }.
POST {{Server_HostAddress}}/api/phi/providers/me/follow-ups/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/reopen
